From bdafdded490c272c535449c5d1c48c30b620e3b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:52:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 077/118] script: a puppet animation's own events (MDLA) reach
 the layer's scripts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An MDLA animation ends with its event list (a u32 and a string each; read as the frame and the
name — Inferred from the layout), which LWE skipped. Now each animation layer's clock fires
animationEvent (event, value) — event {name, frame} — to every script on the image layer when
it passes an event's frame (f / fps): forward, across a loop's wrap (its end, then its start),
back along a mirror; the first step includes frame 0. Before the scripts' init they wait, as
the keyframe timelines' events do. Inferred: WE's runtime for these events wasn't traced; the
d.ts calls AnimationEvent "an animation event fired by puppet or property animations".

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-coverage.md F7 (puppet animationEvent)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
